      "content": "The primary argument against tech giants like Google and Amazon is that their market dominance stifles innovation and unfairly favors their own in-house services through self-preferencing. Conversely, defenders of these companies argue that they are the result of superior merit and that the proposed regulations would stifle free market competition by slowing down their digital transformation. This debate often centers on whether antitrust authorities should proactively intervene to structure the market or wait for natural market forces to correct monopolistic behaviors. Ultimately, the case hinges on balancing the need for fair competition against the risks of over-regulating highly profitable, essential digital platforms.",
